ttps://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/deployments","created_at":"2026-09-30T03:49:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T08:06:36Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-11T08:23:12Z","git_url":"git://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research","homepage":"","size":20247,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["data-weighting","language-models","machine-learning","preregistration","reproducibility"],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":1,"watchers":0,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pulls/6","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/pull/6.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-06T06:46:44Z"},"body":"## Result: matched-progress confirmation (N7) on six fresh WikiText-103 draws\n\nPublishes the result of the study pre-registered in #5, before its runs. The sealed analysis ran once, by the owner, and its labels, intervals and readings are reported as produced.\n\n| Step | 512 − 768 | Label | Mean and 95% interval, df 5 | Draws < 0 / > 0 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **P1** | 1e-4, matched on training NLL | **REVERSAL_CONFIRMED** | +0.00909 [+0.00400, +0.01417] | 0/6 |\n| **S1** | 1e-4, matched on the gap | **CONFIRMED** | +0.00808 [+0.00487, +0.01130] | 0/6 |\n| **S3** | 1e-4, fixed updates | **CONFIRMED** | −0.00454 [−0.00795, −0.00114] | 6/0 |\n| **S4** | 3e-4, matched on training NLL | **CONFIRMED** | +0.01394 [+0.00893, +0.01896] | 0/6 |\n| **S5** | 3e-4, fixed updates | **CONFIRMED** | +0.01382 [+0.01116, +0.01648] | 0/6 |\n| **S2** | 1e-4, matched on validation NLL | **UNAVAILABLE** | Not read: 3 of 6 draws have a reading | Not read |\n\nNOT_OVERFIT in all four arms. No draw is flagged for saturation.\n\n**The sealed reading of the primary:** \"At 1e-4, p* at 512 at E3 is above p* at 768 read at the training NLL 512 reaches at E3 (REVERSAL_CONFIRMED). At fixed updates at E3 on these draws, 768 is above 512, so on these draws the comparison axis reverses the 512-768 ordering at 1e-4. This does not show a capacity mechanism, and nothing about Jane Street's scale follows. Matching on training loss also removes any faster learning of the wider model, so neither axis is privileged.\"\n\n**What this changes:** the evidence status of final claims 4 and 5 (`reports/adversarial-review-response-note-20261106-01/CLAIMS_4_AND_5_STATUS.md`). The strongest post-hoc claim is now a publicly pre-registered, confirmed result, for widths 512 and 768 at 1e-4, on these draws. `RESPONSE.md` is not edited.\n\n**What it does not show:**\n- **On validation NLL at 1e-4 the reversal is not confirmed:** S2 is not read, and it is not evidence either way.\n- **At 3e-4 the ordering does not reverse:** 512 is above 768 on both axes tested.\n- **The fixed-update half is fragile:** S3's interval spans 0 with m03 or m05 left out.\n- **The epoch boundary is a limitation, not pursued.** Panel p\\* rises most just after an epoch boundary, and P1 compares 512 at the end of an epoch with 768 partway through the next. With 768 read at the higher p\\* of its bracket in every draw, P1 is +0.00702 [+0.00216, +0.01189], 5/6 positive (post hoc). Readouts inside E2.0–E2.25 are future work.\n\n**The checks:**\n- `RESULT_VERIFICATION.json`: PASS, with no mismatch in 2,861 comparisons of the outputs or in 1,456 table cells. The verifier and the frozen layout are included.\n- `ASSISTANT_CHECK.md`: a post-hoc assistant recomputation from `POINTS.csv`, not a sealed result.\n- **Neither reaches p\\*, the per-draw losses, E0 or clipping,** which need the run files that only the sealed analysis read.\n- **The results report's layout is not in #5.** It was frozen later, when the losses already existed. That they were unopened rests on local records and the owner's word.\n\n**Redacted, and not byte-identical:** `reports/natural-text-matched-result-20261105-01/RESULT.md` (1). Each local home-path prefix is replaced with `<LOCAL_USER_HOME>`, as for two earlier files, and `PUBLICATION_TRANSFORMATIONS.json` maps the original and public hashes. `RESULT_VERIFICATION.json` names the local `RESULT.md`'s hash, `ac482f31…`. Every other file is byte-identical to its local source.\n\n**Contents:** `reports/natural-text-matched-result-20261105-01/`; `reports/natural-text-matched-analysis-20261105-01/`; the run verifications, the input check and a claim in `reports/natural-text-matched-run-checks-20261104-01/`; Run M1's status result; the owner's exit receipts in `work/natural-text-matched-activation-m1-20261104-01/` and `-m2-`; the frozen layout, the verifier and the input check's script from `reports/natural-text-matched-analysis-approval-20261105-01/`; two owner decision records; `reports/natural-text-matched-assistant-recompute-20261106-01/`; and the note in `reports/adversarial-review-response-note-20261106-01/`.\n\n**Also changed:** a link in the root `README.md`; 1 row in `PUBLICATION_TRANSFORMATIONS.json`; `NATURAL_TEXT_STUDIES.md` (N7 added to the index, the scope and status sections updated, the pre-registration sentence now names #5), `PUBLICATION_NOTES.md` and `DATA_AVAILABILITY.md` (the N7 additions and the published receipts described); and `PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.csv`, with the rows of those five root files updated in place and the new files appended, CRLF endings kept.\n\n**Not included:** the corpus, the run folders, model states and per-sequence arrays; and the analysis's exit receipt, which holds a personal home path and which `RESULT.md` names by hash.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JvfaYmnEddgunH3yg39Yo4)_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research/issues/6/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes